The Android app and its build: SebType's own code, under the MIT licence in ../LICENSE-SebType, except:
- app/src/main/assets/emoji/emoji.txt: made by ../data/emoji/ from Unicode's emoji-test.txt and Unicode CLDR's
  annotations, under the Unicode License v3 (app/src/main/assets/emoji/LICENSE.txt), with SebType's own ASCII
  faces.
- app/src/main/res/font/sebtype_nunito_extrabold.ttf: Nunito, under the SIL Open Font License 1.1
  (../art/fonts/OFL-Nunito.txt).
- app/src/main/res/font/sebtype_pixelify_semibold.ttf: Pixelify Sans, under the SIL Open Font License 1.1
  (../art/fonts/OFL-PixelifySans.txt).
- The data the app's build copies in: the English dictionary and model (../NOTICE), the Chinese data
  (GPL-3.0, ../data/rime) and Mozc's Japanese dictionary (app/mozc-dictionary.sh; Mozc's BSD-3-Clause and its
  data's licences, ../engines/mozc/LICENSE).
- native/src/main/cpp/cmake/: RimeJni's build scripts (MIT, native/src/main/cpp/cmake/LICENSE) with SebType's
  changes; native/NOTICE.md and native/src/main/assets/licenses/ list the libraries native/ builds.
- gradlew, gradlew.bat and gradle/wrapper/: Gradle's wrapper, Apache-2.0.
- test/english/sets/: the English harness's test sets keep their sources' licences (test/english/sets/LICENSE).
  The pristine AOSP LatinIME it builds (Apache-2.0) is fetched at build time, not kept here.

app/src/main/java/org/futo/inputmethod/latin/LatinIME.kt is SebType's own class: only its name is kept from
the FUTO-based app SebType's keyboard replaced (#262), so that an update from it keeps SebType chosen.
